-- Execute-slot events, relative to the middle's scope (TOP.NzeaCore.core.middle).
--
-- These are the events the retire counters cannot answer: the counters say how many, these say when and in what order.
-- The slot is the middle's IS/EX register read side, so the events are watched at the register's own end here. The read
-- that fills it is the issue stage's and its events live beside it (`nzea_core/src/middle/isu/issue.pulse`), as do the
-- write-back stage's (`nzea_core/src/middle/wbu/retire.pulse`); bind them together for the redirect each issued uop
-- turns into (the window is the read/write-back distance, so it is not a fixed number):
--   pulse property --event nzea_core/src/middle/isu/issue.pulse <ISU> Issue \
--       --event nzea_core/src/middle/uop.pulse <MID> Uop \
--       --event nzea_core/src/middle/wbu/retire.pulse <WB> Wbu \
--       --eval 'Uop.uop_issue -> Wbu.redirect'

-- A uop's first cycle in the execute slot: the cycle after the read placed its operands, and the one the units take as
-- the uop's beginning.
uop_issue = slotFirst

-- The slot holds an unfinished uop: the execute stage's occupancy, the cycles it has not released — the uop is
-- presented (`issue_valid`, the slot's read side) and the back has not paced the register yet.
slot_busy = issue_valid && !pace
